<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="band faq" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><div class="eyebrow">Common Questions</div><h2>Straight answers, before you call.</h2></div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details open><summary>Do I need a will or a trust?</summary><p>It depends on what you own and what you want to happen. A will directs where things go; a trust can help your family avoid probate, keep matters private, and plan for incapacity. On your call, Russ will tell you plainly which fits &mdash; and won&rsquo;t upsell you into more than you need.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What&rsquo;s included in the flat fee &mdash; and what isn&rsquo;t?</summary><p>Each plan lists its included documents and guidance. The flat fee covers the legal work in that plan&rsquo;s scope, confirmed in writing before we begin. Court filing fees and third-party costs (for example, recording fees) are separate and disclosed up front.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can everything be handled virtually?</summary><p>Yes. Consultations, review, and most planning are handled virtually, with guided signing. If a step requires an in-person formality, we&rsquo;ll tell you in advance.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you practice in Texas?</summary><p>Russ is licensed in Alabama. If you&rsquo;re outside Alabama, tell us where you&rsquo;re located and we&rsquo;ll confirm exactly how we can help &mdash; often by coordinating with trusted local counsel &mdash; before any engagement begins.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you update an existing plan?</summary><p>Often, yes. Bring what you have; Russ will review it and recommend whether an update or a fresh plan makes more sense for your situation.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if I own a business?</summary><p>That&rsquo;s the Legacy &amp; Business plan &mdash; it coordinates your estate plan with business succession so ownership, control, and your family are all accounted for together.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Does contacting Tercet create an attorney-client relationship?</summary><p>No. Reaching out, or sending information through this site, does not create an attorney-client relationship. That relationship begins only when we both sign a written engagement.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

